  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 143 AM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nMonday night through Friday\nAssessment...high (>80%) confidence of a cool down\n\nA cool front will move through the area Monday night and bring \ntemperatures more in line with normals for mid-October. Compared to \nthe weekend, it will feel chilly.\n\nRain chances will slowly increase the second half of the work week \nas a tropical connection with the Gulf becomes established and a \nsystem moves out of the Rockies. The timing of this system is still \nin question but the model consensus is suggesting Wednesday night \ninto Thursday with the highest rain chances.\n\nA more substantial cold front is progged to move through the area \nFriday night which will usher in below normal temperatures for next \nweekend.",
